<title>USA: Borg-Warner Automotive completes sale.</title>
<headline>Borg-Warner Automotive completes sale.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-01-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Borg-Warner Automotive Inc said Monday it completed the sale of its North American manual transmission manufacturing business to Transmisiones y Equipos Mercanicos S.A. de C.V. on December 31, 1996.</p>
<p>As previously reported, Borg-Warner expects to take a one-time charge of $35 million or $1.50 per share, in the fourth quarter as a result of the sale.</p>
<p>The sale agreement was reached in late October and consummated by yearend as originally planned.</p>
<p>Borg-Warner supplies highly engineered components and systems primarily for automotive drivetrain applications.</p>
<p>	     ((Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
